NAME
       setfont - load a console font

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/cervus.h>

       int cervus_setfont(const void *glyphs, unsigned w, unsigned h,
                          unsigned count, const void *unicode_map);
       int cervus_setfont_reset(void);

DESCRIPTION
       Replaces the console font. The character cell may change size,
       in which case the virtual consoles reflow: their contents are
       preserved, the cursor is repositioned, and SIGWINCH goes to the
       foreground subtree so full-screen programs redraw.

       A Unicode map may be supplied, as PSF2 fonts carry, so that
       UTF-8 output finds the right glyph.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, negative on failure.

SEE ALSO
       setfont(1), ioctl(2)
